 2. 🏀 NBA merry-go-round keeps on spinning 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Aïda Amer/Axios Marc Lore has agreed to sell his controlling stake in the NBA's Minnesota Timberwolves and the WNBA's Minnesota Lynx to billionaire investor Marc Stad at a $4.5 billion enterprise value, Axios' Dan Primack reports. 

 That comes just a week after Mark Walter agreed to sell the Los Angeles Lakers to Joshua Kushner and Bob Iger for $12.5 billion. 🐺 Lore — a serial entrepreneur and former Walmart exec — gained control of the Timberwolves last summer, after a protracted legal process.

 Lore's partner on the deal, ex-MLB player Alex Rodriguez, will remain a part of club ownership. 📆 Behind the scenes: The deal has been in process for several months, per a source familiar — which means it wasn't a reaction to the Lakers sale.

