 4. 🐿️ 1 fun thing: Fat Marmot Week 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 A marmot named 9 sits outside her den on Aug. 6 in Gothic, Colo. Photo: Brittany Peterson/AP Fat Marmot Week is helping scientists drum up donations for their research into the furry ground squirrels living high in the Colorado mountains.

 The riff on Fat Bear Week starts Monday, and comes as federal funding cuts jeopardize the researchers' work. 🔬 The local marmot study, run by UCLA researchers about 20 miles south of Aspen, has been ongoing since 1962 — making it one of the world's longest-running studies of individual mammals.

 The researchers need to bank three years of funding — over $200,000 — to keep working next summer. Go deeper . 

 
 
